      "postID": "644acc9523bf3cf2a017637a",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've run into this same issue - objects I animate the scale of have any child PhysBone components \"disappear\". When emulating with Av3Emulator, it also noticeably spams my console with errors, though I recognize it is not updated to beta. I'll post a picture of the errors anyway.\n\nIn my setup, I have a spawn-in animation for a container, and it scales it in. The PhysBone component is within the armature of a child object of the container. The wings on the bat object disappear, as shown in the attached images. These are both in Unity, with the missing wings when emulated, but this does occur in-game in the beta also.\n\nRemoving the layers with scale animations fixes the issue, and the PhysBone-affected components don't disappear.\n\nI do use Gesture to animate this, and this happens with both PhysBone 1.1 and 1.0.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
